  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The initial mass of a rocket is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>. Calculate at what rate the fuel should be burnt so that the rocket is given an acceleration of,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The gases come out at a relative speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, with respect to the rocket:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mtext>Use</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
    "image": null
